<v Barbara Clinkscales>是的，不，等吃完饭再说。你的节食计划怎么样了？

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.990
<v Tess Clinkscales>Forget my diet. Everybody like me the way I am.
<v Tess Clinkscales>忘掉我的节食计划吧。大家都喜欢我现在的样子。

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:51.300
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Oh Lord. First, she was all depressed. She said her arms was too fat.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>哦天哪。起初，她很沮丧。她说她的手臂太胖了。

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:53.840
<v Tess Clinkscales>They still is. Look, I still want to get my arms sucked.
<v Tess Clinkscales>现在还是。看，我还是想把手臂吸脂。

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:59.490
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Some boy done told her that she looked good, so she don't care about-- she want liposuc-- what you call that?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>有个男孩说她看起来很漂亮，所以她不在乎——她想要抽脂——你管那个叫什么？

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:05.240
<v Tess Clinkscales>My arms sucked. I don't know what it's called. I think it's called liposuction. But I just want to get my arms sucked.
<v Tess Clinkscales>把我的手臂抽脂。我不知道那叫什么。我想叫抽脂手术。但我只想把手臂抽掉脂肪。

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:22.990
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Oh, OK. Go turn that skillet off. I'll go and cook the tacos.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>哦，好的。去把平底锅关掉。我去煮夹饼。

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:35.830
<v Ira Glass>People always ask me, do I have picks with my kids, who I like the most. And people always tell me, I know you're proud of Tess. I know that's your pick. But you know, Tess is not my pick. I don't have a pick.
<v Ira Glass>人们总是问我，我有偏心吗，谁是我最喜欢的孩子。人们总是告诉我，我知道你为泰丝感到骄傲。我知道那是你的最爱。但你知道吗，泰丝并不是我的最爱。我没有最喜欢的。

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:41.610
<v Ira Glass>Angie's not my pick. Gerald is not my pick. I love my kids the same. They all special in they own way.
<v Ira Glass>安吉不是我的最爱。杰拉尔德不是我的最爱。我同样爱我的孩子们。他们每个人都有自己的独特之处。

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:57.650
<v Ira Glass>Angie, I had Angie at 15. And I was a baby having a baby. I was 15. I didn't know nothing about raising kids. I knew nothing about life. But I was determined to stay in school and to graduate and to raise Angie.
<v Ira Glass>安吉，我15岁时生的安吉。我还只是个孩子生孩子。我才15岁。我什么都不懂，关于养育孩子。我对生活一无所知。但我决心留在学校，毕业，抚养安吉。

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:11.150
<v Ira Glass>And it was just me and her against the world. And I did it. Even though she dropped out of school and had babies and everything, but she's still a good person. She's my first born.
<v Ira Glass>那时只有我和她面对整个世界。我做到了。尽管她中途辍学，有了孩子，等等，但她依然是个好人。她是我的长女。

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:25.040
<v Ira Glass>And Gerald is mommy's man. That's my son. All my life, I never had a father. I never had a brother. And so only time I ever loved a man was in a relationship.
<v Ira Glass>而杰拉尔德是妈妈的乖儿子。那是我的儿子。我这辈子，从未有过父亲。我从未有过兄弟。所以我也只在恋爱关系中爱过男人。

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:42.560
<v Ira Glass>And when my son was born, that's a man who loves me unconditionally. His love is just because I'm his momma. It's not because he wants something from me. It's not because he wants sex or something. A man finally loved me for me.
<v Ira Glass>当我儿子出生时，那是一个无条件爱我的男人。他的爱仅仅因为我是他妈妈。不是因为他想要从我这儿得到什么。不是因为他想要性爱什么的。一个男人终于因为我本身而爱我。

00:15:42.560 --> 00:16:00.710
<v Ira Glass>And Tess, she's a carbon copy of me. In other words, she's a young me. And you would think she's my pick, but she's not.
<v Ira Glass>至于泰丝，她是我的翻版。换句话说，她是年轻时的我。你会以为她是我的最爱，但她不是。

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.730
<v Hen 1>Come on, let's make a toast.
<v Hen 1>来吧，干杯。

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:03.620
<v Hen 2>To the Hens.
<v Hen 2>为了母鸡小分队。

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:04.950
<v Hen 1>To the Hens.
<v Hen 1>为了母鸡小分队。

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:09.050
<v Hen 2>Everlasting, never-ending sisters.
<v Hen 2>永恒的，无止尽的姐妹们。

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:19.820
<v Barbara Clinkscales>The Hens are a group of ladies that's been friends since high school. We do all kind of stuff together. We laugh, we talk, we watch movies, we get in trouble.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>母鸡小分队是一群从高中起就是朋友的女士。我们一起做各种事。我们大笑，聊天，看电影，闯祸。

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:22.140
<v Barbara Clinkscales>OK, wait a minute. It spells out something. What do it spell?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>好的，等一下。它拼出了什么。拼出来是什么？

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:26.130
<v Hen 3>Never-ending, everlasting sisters.
<v Hen 3>永恒的，无止尽的姐妹。

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:30.970
<v Barbara Clinkscales>H-E-N-S. H-- hens.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>H-E-N-S。H——母鸡。

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:45.530
<v Ira Glass>Some of the most fun we have is when we go away. We leave the kids, the husbands, the job. We leave everybody. Rent a room, and eat, laugh, and talk, and just don't do nothing. And our next big trip is to Jamaica.
<v Ira Glass>我们最开心的时刻就是去度假。我们放下孩子、丈夫、工作。我们抛下所有人。租个房间，吃饭，大笑，谈天，什么都不做。我们下一次的大旅行是去牙买加。

00:16:45.530 --> 00:17:05.400
<v Ira Glass>And we have been planning and paying for this trip since October of last year. And whenever the Hens are sitting around, talking about our trip to Jamaica, we end up talking about our fantasies, and what we're going to do when we get there. Every Hen has a different fantasy about Jamaica and what they want to do.
<v Ira Glass>自从去年10月以来，我们一直在计划并为这次旅行存钱。每当母鸡们坐在一起谈论我们的牙买加之行时，我们最后总会谈到我们的幻想，以及我们到了那儿要做什么。每个母鸡对牙买加以及她们想做的事都有不同的幻想。

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:32.350
<v Hen 4>My fantasy is on the beach, a big, black piano, with this man in a white jacket, and I name him Sam, playing the piano, playing love songs. Y'all know this? And me leaning over it with a exotic drink. And me constantly saying, "Play it again, Sam."
<v Hen 4>我的幻想是在沙滩上，一台黑色的大钢琴，有一个穿着白外套的男人，我叫他山姆，在弹钢琴，弹着情歌。你们都知道这个吗？我靠在钢琴上，手里拿着一杯异国情调的饮料。我不断地说：“再弹一次，山姆。”

00:17:32.350 --> 00:18:05.490
<v Barbara Clinkscales>When I go out with my girlfriends, and I meet men, and we go out, especially on one of those hoochie mama nights-- hoochie mama can mean a lot of things. Sometimes we'll call ourselves, yeah, we're going to be hoochie mamas tonight. That mean we going to dress sexy. We don't overdo it, just show a little cleavage, a little legs, something with a split. And I go out, and I meet men, they just love me. They just all over me. But they don't know that that's the evil twin, my evil twin.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>当我和闺蜜出去，遇见男人们，我们出去玩，特别是在那些“浪荡女”之夜——浪荡女可能意味着很多事情。有时我们会说，是的，我们今晚要做浪荡女。那意味着我们要打扮得性感。我们不会过度，只是露一点乳沟，一点腿，或者穿件开叉的裙子。我出去遇见男人，他们就爱死我了。他们全都围绕着我。但他们不知道那是邪恶双胞胎，我的邪恶双胞胎。

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:22.900
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Everybody know about my evil twin. One of my coworkers found out about my evil twin, and he laughed because they know Barbara the hard worker, the mom, the grandmother. But every now and then, the evil twin will slip out at work. But when I go out, the men meet the evil twin.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>每个人都知道我的邪恶双胞胎。我的一个同事发现了我的邪恶双胞胎，他笑了，因为他们只知道努力工作的芭芭拉，那个妈妈，那个祖母。但偶尔，邪恶双胞胎会在工作中溜出来。但当我出去时，男人们见到的是邪恶双胞胎。

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:30.020
<v Barbara Clinkscales>The night we get to Jamaica, I'm going to get out on the balcony. And then I'm going to let all them Jamaican men know that I'm there. And I'm going to do the Xena yell.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我们到牙买加的那天晚上，我会走到阳台上。然后我会让那些牙买加男人们知道我在那里。我会发出《战士公主》西娜那样的尖叫。

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:32.410
<v Hen 5>You do that Xena yell, and they're running away.
<v Hen 5>你发出那种西娜尖叫，他们会逃之夭夭的。

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:38.980
<v Barbara Clinkscales>No, baby, not that Xena yell. Barbara standing out on that balcony in that gown, and my hair flowing in the wind, no, baby, nuh-uh.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>不，宝贝，不是那种西娜尖叫。是芭芭拉穿着长袍站在那阳台上，头发在风中飘扬，不，宝贝，没那回事。

00:18:38.980 --> 00:19:04.650
<v Ira Glass>But when they get to know me, when they see that evil twin was just that personality for the moment, that night, out partying, dancing, living. And then they get to know the serious me, the mom, the hard worker, the grandmother, they get kind of turned off. And they constantly refer back to the night we met, that personality.
<v Ira Glass>但当他们真正了解我之后，当他们看出那个邪恶双胞胎只是那一瞬间的性格，那晚出去狂欢、跳舞、生活。然后他们认识了严肃的我，那个妈妈、努力工作的人、祖母，他们就会感到扫兴。他们总是回头谈论我们初次见面的那个夜晚，那种性格。

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:05.660
<v Barbara Clinkscales>What's yours, Tiny?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你的呢，泰尼？

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:06.400
<v Tiny>Mine's is dirty.
<v Tiny>我的很脏。

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:07.460
<v Barbara Clinkscales>It ain't clean, huh?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>不干净是吧？

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.120
<v Tiny>It ain't clean.
<v Tiny>不干净。

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:47.560
<v Barbara Clinkscales>I know when I talk to them on the phone after we have met. And they call me up, and I try to have decent conversations with them. And they want to know, "How do you make love? What's your favorite position? How often do you like to make love?" I'm like, "That's none of your business." I'm like, "Do you have kids? Where you work at? Are you religious?" I want to talk about these things, and they get turned off. They don't want to talk anymore.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我知道在我们见面后，我在电话里和他们聊天。他们给我打电话，我试着和他们进行体面的谈话。而他们想知道：“你是怎么做爱的？你最喜欢的姿势是什么？你喜欢多久做一次爱？”我就说：“那不关你的事。”我说：“你有孩子吗？你在哪儿工作？你有宗教信仰吗？”我想谈论这些事情，他们就失去了兴趣。他们不想再聊了。

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.330
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Leah, what's your fantasy?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>莉亚，你的幻想是什么？

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:54.000
<v Leah>When we go to Jamaica? Oh, just to make wild, passionate love.
<v Leah>当我们去牙买加的时候？哦，就是进行一场疯狂、充满激情的性爱。

00:19:54.000 --> 00:20:24.370
<v Barbara Clinkscales>My girlfriend, Peaches, she's going through the same thing I'm going through. And we said, we have PhDs in heartbreak. We can write a book on "No, that's not it." And we just sit up and we laugh and we talk. And we always tell each other, "Well, one day, we going to be at each other's wedding. We going to be standing up there, looking at each other walk down the aisle in love and happy."
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我的好朋友皮奇斯，她正在经历和我一样的事。我们说，我们在心碎方面都有博士学位。我们可以写一本书叫《不，那不是真的》。我们就坐在那儿大笑，聊天。我们总是告诉对方：“嗯，有一天，我们要参加彼此的婚礼。我们要站在那儿，看着彼此穿着婚纱走过过道，坠入爱河，幸福美满。”

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:35.380
<v Barbara Clinkscales>And so why are we here? We sit up and talk about our PhDs. And we add a new chapter to our book. It just doesn't seem to fail. I don't know.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>那么我们为什么要在这儿呢？我们坐着谈论我们的博士学位。然后我们又给我们的书加了新章节。这似乎没完没了。我不知道。

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.300
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Come on, Rosetta.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>来吧，罗塞塔。

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:39.290
<v Rosetta>Oh no, mine's is too, too, too outrageous.
<v Rosetta>哦不，我的太……太离谱了。

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:40.800
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Well, tell one of the nice things.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>好吧，讲一点点好的部分。

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:45.030
<v Rosetta>I don't have nice things like that. I have great fantasies, great fantasies.
<v Rosetta>我没有那种好的东西。我有伟大的幻想，伟大的幻想。

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.290
<v Hen 6>Just a walk on the beach.
<v Hen 6>就只是在沙滩上散散步。

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:54.010
<v Rosetta>They cannot be told.
<v Rosetta>不能说。

00:20:54.010 --> 00:21:15.580
<v Barbara Clinkscales>It's Monday morning. Tess has gone to school. We're running late, so I called a cab. I called the livery. It's like a person owning his own car, and he drive it as a cab. These cab companies only work throughout the black neighborhood.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>是周一早上。泰丝已经去学校了。我们迟到了，所以我叫了一辆出租车。我叫了私人租赁车。就像一个人拥有自己的车，当出租车开。这些出租车公司只在黑人社区内运营。

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:56.370
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Gerald, did you get you a bus pass? Your school ID? Did you ever find your school ID? OK. Did you lock those bars? You turn off the iron? So I'm going to go downstairs and wait on the cab. They said, four minutes. A grate leaking. Come on, Gerald.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>杰拉尔德，你买公交月票了吗？你的学生证？你找到学生证了吗？好的。你锁上那些护栏了吗？你把熨斗关了吗？所以我要下楼等车。他们说四分钟。有个地沟漏了。快点，杰拉尔德。

00:21:56.370 --> 00:22:06.590
<v Ira Glass>I'm in the living room with Gerald. I'm just getting home from work. He was watching TV, so I thought I'd talk with him.
<v Ira Glass>我正和杰拉尔德在客厅。刚下班回来。他在看电视，所以我想到跟他聊聊。

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:08.120
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Have you been cutting any more classes?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你还有旷课吗？

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:11.650
<v Gerald Clinkscales>No.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>没。

00:22:11.650 --> 00:22:13.650
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Do you still hate that school?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你还讨厌那个学校吗？

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:14.270
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Yeah.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>是啊。

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:15.770
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Why?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>为什么？

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:17.990
<v Gerald Clinkscales>People start so much stuff.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>人们老爱惹事。

00:22:17.990 --> 00:22:19.730
<v Barbara Clinkscales>What kind of stuff do they start?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>他们惹什么事？

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:25.140
<v Gerald Clinkscales>They be talking stuff. If I do talk back, they act like they about to jump on me.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>他们老是嚼舌根。如果我回嘴，他们就像要扑上来揍我一样。

00:22:25.140 --> 00:22:27.610
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Would they be thinking about jumping you outside?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>他们会想在外面围堵你吗？

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:31.680
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Yeah. They kill people.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>是啊。他们会杀人的。

00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:32.650
<v Barbara Clinkscales>I know.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我知道。

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:33.940
<v Gerald Clinkscales>That's what they talking about doing.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>他们谈论的就是要做那事。

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:35.420
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Killing you?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>杀你？

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:38.080
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Yeah.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>是啊。

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:40.060
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Just for talking back?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>就因为回嘴？

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:42.940
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Yeah.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>是啊。

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:44.950
<v Barbara Clinkscales>What do they say to you?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>他们对你说了什么？

00:22:44.950 --> 00:22:46.530
<v Gerald Clinkscales>They just be starting stuff.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>他们就是爱找茬。

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:48.650
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Like what? Just out of the--
<v Barbara Clinkscales>比如什么？就平白无故地——

00:22:48.650 --> 00:22:59.760
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Like they call you names. And I call them back. And they be like-- they jump hard, and I jump hard back. Five more guys come up on me, telling me, what y'all want to do then?
<v Gerald Clinkscales>比如他们叫你难听的绰号。我也回骂。他们就——他们开始挑衅，我也回击。又有五个人冲上来，问我，你们想怎么样？

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:01.740
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Jump hard? What you mean jump hard?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>开始挑衅？挑衅是什么意思？

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:04.860
<v Gerald Clinkscales>This means they-- you know--
<v Gerald Clinkscales>就是他们——你知道——

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:05.720
<v Barbara Clinkscales>They ready to fight?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>他们准备打架了？

00:23:05.720 --> 00:23:06.590
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Yeah.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>是啊。

00:23:06.590 --> 00:23:08.910
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Jump hard mean they jump up to you with their fists up in--
<v Barbara Clinkscales>挑衅意思就是他们挥着拳头冲到你面前——

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:12.250
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Yeah, they want to pull it. That mean they want to fight you.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>是啊，他们想动手。意思就是他们想跟你打架。

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:13.280
<v Barbara Clinkscales>They want to pull it.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>他们想动手。

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:31.790
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Yeah, that's slang for they want to fight you. That's why I was cutting a few classes. Because if I did when I went to school, I probably would have been beat up by now.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>是啊，那是想跟你打架的俚语。所以我才旷了几节课。因为如果我去学校，我现在可能已经被打了一顿了。

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:45.850
<v Gerald Clinkscales>[SOUND OF SOMEONE MAKING A TELEPHONE CALL]
<v Gerald Clinkscales>[拨打电话的声音]

00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:47.910
<v Marvin Craig>Hello?
<v Marvin Craig>喂？

00:23:47.910 --> 00:23:51.110
<v Barbara Clinkscales>May I speak to Marvin? How you doing?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我能跟马文说话吗？你好吗？

00:23:51.110 --> 00:24:37.450
<v Ira Glass>Marvin. I met Marvin through my Auntie Susie's boyfriend, Grantey. Grantey is from Jamaica And he's been telling me about his nephew, Marvin, and Jamaica for a long, long time. He always told me that Marvin would be the perfect, perfect man for me. But I never paid him any attention. And one Sunday morning, Grantey called me around 7 o'clock in the morning, saying, he just got back from Jamaica, and he had pictures and a phone number, and his nephew wanted me to call him. And I laid in bed, and I tried to go back to sleep, but I couldn't. I couldn't go back to sleep.
<v Ira Glass>马文。我通过姨妈苏西的男朋友格兰提认识了马文。格兰提来自牙买加，他一直跟我提起他的侄子马文和牙买加。他总是说马文是我的完美伴侣。但我从来没在意。有一个周日早上，格兰提在早上7点左右打电话给我，说他刚从牙买加回来，有照片和电话号码，他侄子想让我给他打电话。我躺在床上，试着睡个回笼觉，但我睡不着。我再也睡不着了。

00:24:37.450 --> 00:24:46.040
<v Barbara Clinkscales>That's your favorite picture of me? You have it with you? OK.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>那是你最喜欢我的照片？你随身带着吗？好的。

00:24:46.040 --> 00:24:57.040
<v Ira Glass>So I called him. And when I heard his voice, I went into a trance. It was like I knew him all my life. This was the man for me.
<v Ira Glass>所以我给他打了电话。当我听到他的声音时，我进入了一种恍惚状态。感觉就像我认识他一辈子了。这就是我要找的男人。

00:24:57.040 --> 00:25:07.690
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Yeah, I love that song. Ooh, I used to cry over that song. You do? Well, I got to play it. I want to see you cry.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>是的，我喜欢那首歌。哦，我曾经因为那首歌哭过。你也是？好吧，我得放一放。我想看你哭。

00:25:07.690 --> 00:25:46.950
<v Ira Glass>After talking to Marvin for about a week, he asked me to come to Jamaica. And I got real scared because talking to him on the phone is a security blanket because we're on the phone. We're not in person. And I'm older than him. Marvin, he's 28. I'm 41. And being an older woman, being full-figured, and what if I get there, and he don't like me because I'm older, because I'm a full-figured woman?
<v Ira Glass>和马文聊了大约一周后，他邀请我去牙买加。我真的很害怕，因为在电话里和他说话有一种安全感，因为我们在电话里。我们没有面对面。而且我比他大。马文，他28岁。我41岁。作为一个大龄女性，又是丰满体型，如果我到了那儿，他因为我年纪大、因为我身材丰满而不喜欢我怎么办？

00:25:46.950 --> 00:25:50.470
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Those songs make you cry just like they make me cry.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>那些歌让你哭，就像让我哭一样。

00:25:50.470 --> 00:26:10.280
<v Ira Glass>When I tell him these things, he know how I feel. But he says, it don't matter. He fell in love with my personality, the way I think, and the things that I believe in. He said, it really don't matter. So it's time. I'm going to Jamaica. It's June 6.
<v Ira Glass>当我告诉他这些事时，他知道我的感受。但他却说，那不重要。他爱上的是我的个性、我的思考方式，以及我的信仰。他说，那真的不重要。所以是时候了。我要去牙买加。现在是6月6日。

00:26:10.280 --> 00:26:37.480
<v Barbara Clinkscales>I love you too, baby. Yeah. Bye. Here, Gerald, get the keys. I forgot the flowers. What's that, Gerald? Where the flowers? The bag is on the microwave that-- Gerald.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我也爱你，宝贝。好的。再见。来，杰拉尔德，拿钥匙。我忘了花。那是什吗，杰拉尔德？花在哪儿？袋子在微波炉上，那个——杰拉尔德。

00:26:37.480 --> 00:26:38.690
<v Young Boy>What you gonna do?
<v Young Boy>你要做什么？

00:26:38.690 --> 00:26:42.450
<v Barbara Clinkscales>We getting ready to go see Gerald go on his girlfriend's prom.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我们要准备去看杰拉尔德参加他女朋友的毕业舞会。

00:26:42.450 --> 00:26:43.460
<v Young Boy>With Keisha?
<v Young Boy>和基莎一起？

00:26:43.460 --> 00:26:50.080
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Yeah.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>是啊。

00:26:50.080 --> 00:26:58.370
<v Ira Glass>I never want to prom because I couldn't afford it really. I really couldn't afford it.
<v Ira Glass>我从来没参加过舞会，因为我真的负担不起。我真的负担不起。

00:26:58.370 --> 00:26:59.300
<v Baby>Mamma.
<v Baby>妈妈。

00:26:59.300 --> 00:26:59.930
<v Barbara Clinkscales>What?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>什么？

00:26:59.930 --> 00:27:01.910
<v Baby>That's the dog that bite me.
<v Baby>那就是咬我的那只狗。

00:27:01.910 --> 00:27:05.080
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Yeah, that dog gonna bite you. Now get in the car.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>是啊，那只狗会咬你的。快上车。

00:27:05.080 --> 00:27:21.940
<v Ira Glass>I always wanted it. I said, my kids is going to do the things that I didn't do. And when Angie didn't graduate from high school, it hurt me so bad. I was like, oh God, my kid's going to follow in my footstep. And then with Tess and Gerald, and I made a pact with them, and I made a pact with God that they going to do  this. They going to do it for me, and they going to do it for them.
<v Ira Glass>我一直想要那种体验。我说，我的孩子们要去做我没做过的事。当安吉没能高中毕业时，我太伤心了。我就想，哦上帝，我的孩子要走我的老路了。然后是泰丝和杰拉尔德，我和他们定了一个契约，我和上帝也定了一个契约，他们会完成这个目标的。他们会为我做到，也会为他们自己做到。

00:27:21.940 --> 00:27:34.590
<v Angie>What's wrong, Gerald? You nervous? Huh, Gerald? Look how he holding the flowers like they're a little, bitty baby. You nervous, Gerald?
<v Angie>怎么了，杰拉尔德？你紧张吗？哈，杰拉尔德？看他拿着花的样子，像拿着个小婴儿似的。你紧张吗，杰拉尔德？

00:27:34.590 --> 00:27:35.020
<v Gerald>Nuh-uh.
<v Gerald>没有。

00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:37.190
<v Angie>You're not nervous?
<v Angie>你不紧张？

00:27:37.190 --> 00:27:52.900
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Because I told Tess, I said, your prom dress is going to be rent. Your shoes gonna probably be the phone and light bill. We're not going to have any food that month, and we might have to live in a shelter. Because I'm not paying no bills when it come time for her to go to prom.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>因为我告诉泰丝了，我说，你的舞会礼服会是租的。你的鞋子大概会花掉电话费和电费。那个月我们没饭吃，还可能得住收容所。因为在她去参加舞会的时候，我不会去付任何账单的。

00:27:52.900 --> 00:27:55.500
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Lock the doors. Put the locks on.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>把门锁好。把锁扣上。

00:27:55.500 --> 00:28:24.730
<v Ira Glass>Angie and her friends are talking about crashing the prom, take pictures of Gerald sitting at the table, take pictures of Gerald dancing on the floor, take pictures of Gerald taking pictures. We're so excited. It's not even his prom. But we're going to live our dreams through the twins.
<v Ira Glass>安吉和她的朋友们在谈论去舞会捣乱，给杰拉尔德坐在桌边拍照，给杰拉尔德在舞池跳舞拍照，给拍照的杰拉尔德拍照。我们太兴奋了。尽管那甚至不是他的毕业舞会。但我们要通过这对双胞胎来实现我们的梦想。

00:28:24.730 --> 00:28:33.340
<v Ira Glass>OK. We're standing outside of Keisha's house. Gerald's ringing the doorbell.
<v Ira Glass>好的。我们站在基莎家外面。杰拉尔德在按门铃。

00:28:33.340 --> 00:28:35.680
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Do you have your socks, Gerald?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你带袜子了吗，杰拉尔德？

00:28:35.680 --> 00:29:03.730
<v Ira Glass>Gerald's going to get dressed at her house. He don't have his tux on. I fantasize about Gerald being a man all the time, being a father, working. I have these pictures in my mind, what he's going to look like when he's 30. I don't do this with Angie. I never did this with Tess. But I wonder all the time about Gerald, what he's going to be like when he's a man.
<v Ira Glass>杰拉尔德要去她家换衣服。他还没穿上礼服呢。我总是幻想着杰拉尔德成为男人，成为父亲，工作的样子。我的脑海里有这些画面，想象他30岁时是什么样子。我不会对安吉这样。我以前对泰丝也从没这样过。但我一直都在想杰拉尔德，当他成为男人时会是什么样子。

00:29:03.730 --> 00:29:14.560
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Give her your tux and stuff, Gerald. Don't smash your flower. Give her your tux. Uh-oh. Pick your jacket up, Gerald. Come on now. Don't let it hit the ground.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>把你的礼服和东西给她，杰拉尔德。别弄坏了花。把礼服给她。哦不。捡起你的外套，杰拉尔德。快点。别让它掉在地上。

00:29:14.560 --> 00:29:25.600
<v Ira Glass>Gerald don't have a will like Tess do. Sometime I think Tess took it all from him. But I know somewhere down the line, Gerald's gonna fool me. I know it.
<v Ira Glass>杰拉尔德没有泰丝那种坚强的意志。有时我觉得泰丝把他的意志全抢走了。但我知道在未来的某一天，杰拉尔德会让我大吃一惊的。我知道。

00:29:25.600 --> 00:29:26.240
<v Barbara Clinkscales>She's coming down.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>她下来了。

00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:27.260
<v Gerald Clinkscales>One more, hurry up.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>再来一张，快点。

00:29:27.260 --> 00:29:34.680
<v Barbara Clinkscales>OK. Now she can come down. Oh my goodness. Oh God, she's so pretty.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>好的。现在她可以下来了。哦我的天哪。哦上帝，她太漂亮了。

00:29:34.680 --> 00:29:43.610
<v Barbara Clinkscales>OK, hold it, Gerald. OK, how you gonna pose? Come on. Come on, Gerald. Put your-- yeah, like that. OK, open your-- yeah, yeah, go-- Oh, look at my baby.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>好的，保持住，杰拉尔德。好的，你要怎么摆姿势？快点。快点，杰拉尔德。放你的——对，就像那样。好的，张开你的——对，对，去——哦，看我的宝贝。

00:29:43.610 --> 00:30:00.250
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Oh, look at him. Oh, look at my baby. Hold it again. Hold it again, Gerald. Quickly, hold it like that. Open your-- relax, Gerald. Your hands, relax, there you go.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>哦，看着他。哦，看我的宝贝。再保持住。再保持住，杰拉尔德。快，就这样保持住。张开你的——放松，杰拉尔德。你的手，放松，这就对了。

00:30:00.250 --> 00:30:10.640
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Wait, fix his jacket, fix his jacket. Close your jacket in. OK, there you go. OK, now you go. Relax. There you go, Gerald, relax. OK.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>等等，整理一下他的外套，整理一下他的外套。把外套扣好。好的，这就对了。好的，现在你去吧。放松。这就对了，杰拉尔德，放松。

00:30:10.640 --> 00:30:20.340
<v Ira Glass>One day I'm going to look up, and Gerald's going to outdo Tess. And I'm going to go, "Hey, mommy's man, look at you, boy. You go, boy. That's mommy's man, hey."
<v Ira Glass>有一天我会抬头一看，杰拉尔德会超过泰丝的。我会说，“嘿，妈妈的乖儿子，看看你，小伙子。去吧，孩子。那是妈妈的乖儿子，嘿。”

00:30:20.340 --> 00:30:32.540
<v Barbara Clinkscales>This is not happening to me. This is a movie. I'm dreaming. Somebody pinch me. Wake me up. This don't happen to me, no. I don't supposed to be at this moment. I shouldn't be this happy and this here proud.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>这事不是真的发生在我身上。这是一部电影。我在做梦。谁来掐我一下。叫醒我。这不该发生在我身上，不。我不该处于这一刻。我不该这么快乐，这么自豪。

00:30:32.540 --> 00:30:40.750
<v Ira Glass>I know it. One day, he's going to really fool me. I claim it in your name, God. In your name, Lord, I claim it.
<v Ira Glass>我知道。有一天，他真的会让我大吃一惊的。我以你的名义宣告，上帝。以你的名义，主啊，我宣告。

00:30:40.750 --> 00:30:49.250
<v Ira Glass>[SOUNDS OF BARBARA LAUGHING AND CRYING AT KEISHA'S HOUSE]
<v Ira Glass>[基莎家芭芭拉又笑又哭的声音]

00:30:49.250 --> 00:31:10.190
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Oh, look at that.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>哦，看看那个。

00:31:10.190 --> 00:31:25.390
<v Ira Glass>I'm home. My girls came and picked me up from the airport. And I haven't woke up from this dream yet. So maybe it's not a dream.
<v Ira Glass>我到家了。我女儿们开车去机场接我。我还从没从这个梦里醒来。所以也许这不是梦。

00:31:25.390 --> 00:31:51.990
<v Ira Glass>It's late. Let me look at the time. It's like 2:00 AM. So I've been laying here for about an hour and a half, thinking about the last 11 days of my life in Jamaica with Marvin. Marvin Malcolm Craig.
<v Ira Glass>很晚了。让我看下时间。大概凌晨2点。所以我已经躺在这儿一个半小时了，思考着我在牙买加和马文度过的最后11天。马文·马尔科姆·克雷格。

00:31:51.990 --> 00:32:35.740
<v Ira Glass>Marvin. He's 29 years old. Yes, and I'm 41. When I saw the movie How Stella Got Her Groove Back, I made my daughter Angie promise she wouldn't date over a certain age, and I wouldn't date under a certain age because we would never bump heads dating. And who breaks the promise? Me.
<v Ira Glass>马文。他29岁。是的，而我41岁。当我看那部电影《快乐的斯特拉》时，我让女儿安吉答应我，她绝不和年龄差距过大的人约会，我也绝不和年龄太小的人约会，这样我们就不会在约会问题上产生分歧。结果是谁打破了诺言？是我。

00:32:35.740 --> 00:33:08.390
<v Ira Glass>I can't believe it. My daughter will be 26 in November. And March-- let's see, November, December, January, February, March. So he's a year and four months older than my daughter. No, two years, four months. Oh boy. Well, I don't care.
<v Ira Glass>我简直不敢相信。我女儿11月就26岁了。而三月——让我们看看，11月、12月、1月、2月、3月。所以他比我女儿大一岁零四个月。不，两岁零四个月。哦天哪。嗯，我不在乎。

00:33:08.390 --> 00:33:41.530
