<v Ira Glass>And he said, "Come, Barbara. Come get in the shower." I did not want to do that. Because I would not let him see me without my clothes on because I feel my body was so ugly, stretch marks from having kids, being a full-figured woman. I know, look at your beautiful body, breasts sit up all perfect. And I sat there, holding my stomach, holding my breath.
<v Ira Glass>他说：“来，芭芭拉。来洗澡吧。”我不想那样做。因为我不想让他看见我没穿衣服的样子，因为我觉得我的身体太丑了，生孩子留下的妊娠纹，作为丰满女性的体型。我知道，看看你美丽的身体，乳房耸立得那么完美。我坐在那儿，收着肚子，屏住呼吸。

