<v Gerald Clinkscales>我妈待在家里。我们谈过了。她问我怎么想。我说，我想留下孩子，但她也知道我不会去学校。

00:49:50.340 --> 00:50:08.440
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Hey, block that out. Shh. Don't tell my momma. Block that out. I don't want the world to know I'm not going to school. But I'll change now, seeing as I got a kid on the way.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>嘿，把那句删掉。嘘。别告诉我妈。删掉那句。我不想让全世界都知道我没去学校。但我会改变的，既然我有孩子了。

00:50:08.440 --> 00:50:23.400
<v Gerald Clinkscales>I just need a job. That's what I need. But it's hard. They be thinking I'm not trying. Ma, don't think I'm not trying this hard because my girl, Keisha, she type me up some resumes.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>我只需要一份工作。那是我需要的。但这太难了。他们觉得我没在努力。妈，别觉得我没在努力，因为我女朋友基莎，她帮我打了几份简历。

00:50:23.400 --> 00:50:33.140
<v Gerald Clinkscales>Shoot. So I went out there, I gave them the resumes. And they acting like they bored. So I'm like, man. I'm calling back like, "You checked over my application or whatever?"
<v Gerald Clinkscales>该死。所以我出去了，把简历给了他们。他们表现得好像很无聊。所以我心想，伙计。我打电话过去说：“你们看我的申请了吗？”

00:50:33.140 --> 00:50:58.800
<v Gerald Clinkscales>He's like, "Yeah, I'll call you. I'll call you. I'll call you back next week." And hear you, I'll be two weeks later, calling back. So that's it. It's messed up for me right now.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>他回答说：“是啊，我会给你打电话。我会给你打电话。我下周给你回电。”你听着，两周都过去了，我还在打电话。就是这样。我现在处境很糟糕。

00:50:58.800 --> 00:51:56.910
<v Gerald Clinkscales>People are acting like they don't want to help nobody and stuff, acting all shisty. It's hot in here. It's 90, almost 100 degrees. Hot, sweaty, talking on microphones, stomach hurt, feel like I'm about to throw up. Talking to you about my personal life. I'm really messed up. But I messed up. Now I got to pay the price. But I just messed up. It'd be different if I didn't have no kid on the way. It's just messed up for me.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>人们表现得好像不想帮任何人一样，表现得都很势利。这儿太热了。90度，快100度了。热得汗流浃背，对着麦克风说话，胃痛，感觉快要吐了。跟你谈论我的私人生活。我真的搞砸了。但我搞砸了。现在我得付出代价。但我确实搞砸了。如果我没有孩子，那会是另一回事。但我现在的处境真的很糟。

00:51:56.910 --> 00:51:58.910
<v Female Friend>The bar is open.
<v Female Friend>酒吧开放了。

00:51:58.910 --> 00:52:08.170
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Today is my bridal shower. All the Hens are coming. My family, my mom is coming. My aunt, her sister, their friends.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>今天是我的新娘送礼会。母鸡们都要来。我的家人，我妈要来。我姨妈，她姐妹，她们的朋友。

00:52:08.170 --> 00:52:14.600
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Hey Caroline, hey girl.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>嘿卡罗琳，嘿女孩。

00:52:14.600 --> 00:52:18.860
<v Ira Glass>My nieces, my daughter's friends are coming to my bridal shower, and Rambo.
<v Ira Glass>我的侄女们，我女儿的朋友都要来参加我的送礼会，还有兰博。

00:52:18.860 --> 00:52:23.250
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Y'all got your dollars ready? Your 5's and 10's?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你们准备好美元了吗？你们的5元和10元纸币？

00:52:23.250 --> 00:52:43.350
<v Ira Glass>Rambo is the stripper. He's coming all the way from Atlanta, Georgia. And he comes out in this expensive Armani suit, walking around, eyeballing the women, and talking business to them. So everybody, we've been practicing, "Rambo, Rambo, Rambo." Then we going to do the Xena yell, "La-la-la-la."
<v Ira Glass>兰博是脱衣舞男。他远道从佐治亚州亚特兰大过来。他穿着昂贵的阿玛尼西装出场，走来走去，盯着女人们看，跟她们谈生意。所以大家，我们一直在练习，“兰博，兰博，兰博”。然后我们要发出西娜尖叫，“啦-啦-啦-啦”。

00:52:43.350 --> 00:52:56.270
<v Barbara's Sister>So this is Jeri Bello. And I invited Jeri today to pray over this, to pray for my sister to be happy with her new husband. So that's why I invited Jeri here today. Now I'm going to turn it over to Jeri Bello.
<v Barbara's Sister>这位是杰里·贝洛。我今天邀请杰里来为这一切祈祷，为我妹妹能和新丈夫幸福祈祷。这就是我今天邀请杰里的原因。现在我把时间交给杰里·贝洛。

00:52:56.270 --> 00:53:21.890
<v Jeri Bello>God bless everybody here. Well, I give honor to God today and to the future bride, the future groom in his absence. I just want to share a word, and it's on marriage. A sacrament is an act instituted by God for us to observe, so that we, the people, can receive divine strength.
<v Jeri Bello>上帝保佑在座的各位。好吧，今天我向上帝表达敬意，也向未来的新娘、缺席的未来新郎表达敬意。我只是想分享一句话，关于婚姻。圣事是上帝为我们设立的行为，以便我们所有人都能获得神圣的力量。

00:53:21.890 --> 00:53:25.380
<v Jeri Bello>[SOUND OF THE XENA YELL]
<v Jeri Bello>[西娜尖叫声]

00:53:25.380 --> 00:53:32.350
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Come on, y'all. Rambo. Rambo. Rambo. Rambo. Rambo.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>来吧，各位。兰博。兰博。兰博。兰博。兰博。

00:53:32.350 --> 00:53:55.810
<v Barbara Clinkscales>[SOUND OF WOMEN YELLING AND CHEERING]
<v Barbara Clinkscales>[女人们的尖叫和欢呼声]

00:53:55.810 --> 00:53:59.910
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Tell me what you think about your baby and the pictures.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>告诉我你对你的孩子和那些照片怎么看。

00:53:59.910 --> 00:54:08.660
<v Ira Glass>I have ultrasound pictures of Gerald's baby. It's a girl. Gerald's going to have a little girl.
<v Ira Glass>我有杰拉尔德孩子的超声波照片。是个女孩。杰拉尔德要有个小女儿了。

00:54:08.660 --> 00:54:10.940
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Who's she look like to you?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>在你看来她像谁？

00:54:10.940 --> 00:54:15.460
<v Gerald Clinkscales>People saying that she look like me by the nose and the lips.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>人们说从鼻子和嘴唇看她像我。

00:54:15.460 --> 00:54:24.780
<v Barbara Clinkscales>She sure do.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>确实很像。

00:54:24.780 --> 00:54:32.270
<v Ira Glass>She's big. You can see her head, her nose, and her lip. And she look like she got fat cheeks.
<v Ira Glass>她很大。你能看到她的头、鼻子和嘴唇。看起来她有胖乎乎的脸颊。

00:54:32.270 --> 00:54:38.420
<v Barbara Clinkscales>How you feel about having a baby girl on the way?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你对于即将有个小女儿是什么感觉？

00:54:38.420 --> 00:54:41.380
<v Gerald Clinkscales>It feel OK.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>感觉还行。

00:54:41.380 --> 00:54:53.980
<v Barbara Clinkscales>I have to say, I'm kind of excited. I'm not so depressed like I used to be when I thought about Gerald being a father. I guess with babies, when you see the babies, it makes it all right.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我得说，我有点兴奋。我不像以前想杰拉尔德当爸爸时那么沮丧了。我想对于婴儿，当你看到婴儿时，一切就都好了。

00:54:53.980 --> 00:54:59.140
<v Barbara Clinkscales>So what are you going to do? How you going to be a father? What type of father are you going to be?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>那你打算怎么办？你打算怎么当爸爸？你会成为什么样的父亲？

00:54:59.140 --> 00:55:01.090
<v Gerald Clinkscales>A good father.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>一个好父亲。

00:55:01.090 --> 00:55:04.460
<v Barbara Clinkscales>What is your definition of a good father?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你对好父亲的定义是什么？

00:55:04.460 --> 00:55:09.780
<v Gerald Clinkscales>To be there for my baby like a father should do.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>像父亲应该做的那样陪伴我的孩子。

00:55:09.780 --> 00:55:13.310
<v Barbara Clinkscales>What should a father do? You tell me. What should a father do?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>父亲应该做什么？你告诉我。父亲应该做什么？

00:55:13.310 --> 00:55:32.610
<v Gerald Clinkscales>I don't know. Like the fathers on TV, I guess. I don't know yet.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>我不知道。就像电视里的父亲吧，我想。我还没想好。

00:55:32.610 --> 00:55:51.210
<v Barbara Clinkscales>I told Gerald when I get some extra money, I'm going to take him shopping and get things, so he can feel good about himself. Because he kind of lost it the other day. Kind of scared me too, the way he was crying. Because he is no longer in the STEP program.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我告诉杰拉尔德，等我有额外的钱，我要带他去购物买东西，这样他能感觉好点。因为他那天有点失控了。他哭的时候也把我吓坏了。因为他不再是STEP项目的成员了。

00:55:51.210 --> 00:56:09.260
<v Barbara Clinkscales>He's in regular classes because his test scores were so high. And he says, "The classes are too hard. They're too hard. I can't do it. I got a baby on the way. I don't know. I don't think I'm a dummy." And he was just going on and on and just scaring the hell out of me.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>他在普通班上课，因为他的考试成绩太高了。他说：“课程太难了。太难了。我做不到。我有孩子要出生了。我不知道。我不觉得我是个笨蛋。”他一直在说，真的快把我吓死了。

00:56:09.260 --> 00:56:10.610
<v Barbara Clinkscales>Are you scared?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>你害怕吗？

00:56:10.610 --> 00:56:17.080
<v Gerald Clinkscales>I don't know. I still like that. I'm kind of ready though.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>我不知道。我还是喜欢那样。不过我已经准备好了。

00:56:17.080 --> 00:56:30.260
<v Barbara Clinkscales>But I let him know that everybody goes through that. And he's going to make it. All he had to do was study harder and don't give up. And I know he's going to turn out to be a  good father.
<v Barbara Clinkscales>但我让他知道每个人都会经历那个阶段。他会成功的。他所要做的就是更努力学习，别放弃。我知道他会成为一个好父亲的。

00:56:30.260 --> 00:56:34.390
<v Barbara Clinkscales>When you look at those pictures, what do you think?
<v Barbara Clinkscales>当你看着那些照片时，你在想什么？

00:56:34.390 --> 00:56:47.410
<v Gerald Clinkscales>I can't wait. That's what I think. I can't wait 'til the baby comes.
<v Gerald Clinkscales>我迫不及待了。这就是我想的。我迫不及待等到孩子出生了。

00:56:47.410 --> 00:57:13.090
<v Barbara Clinkscales>And I told him, "I got your back. I'm gonna do what I can. Don't worry. Momma got your back."
<v Barbara Clinkscales>我告诉他：“我会支持你的。我会尽我所能。别担心。妈妈支持你。”

00:57:13.090 --> 00:57:29.200
<v Ira Glass>That story was recorded by Barbara Clinkscales and was produced by Elise Spiegel with funding from the Corporation for Public Broadcasting. Gerald is currently speaking with Keisha's family again. They're sitting here in the studio with me as I say these words. She looks great. Her baby is due the first week of the new millennium.
<v Ira Glass>那个故事是由芭芭拉·克林克斯凯尔斯录制的，由伊莉丝·斯皮格尔制作，并获得了公共广播公司的资金支持。杰拉尔德目前正在和基莎的家人沟通。当我录下这些话时，他们正和我坐在一起。她看起来棒极了。她的预产期在新千年的第一周。

00:57:29.200 --> 00:57:41.010
